<article class="env-definition" id="08RT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08RT">Definition <span data-tag="08RT">17.28.10</span>.</a> Let $(f, f^\sharp ) : (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (S, \mathcal{O}_ S)$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. An <em>$S$-derivation</em> into $\mathcal{F}$ is a $f^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ S$-derivation, or more precisely a $f^\sharp $-derivation in the sense of Definition <a href="/tag/01UN" data-tag="01UN">17.28.1</a>. We denote $\text{Der}_ S(\mathcal{O}_ X, \mathcal{F})$ the set of $S$-derivations into $\mathcal{F}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>sheaf of differentials $\Omega _{X/S}$ of $X$ over $S$</em> is the module of differentials $\Omega _{\mathcal{O}_ X/f^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ S}$ endowed with its universal $S$-derivation $\text{d}_{X/S} : \mathcal{O}_ X \to \Omega _{X/S}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>